data.content:
**No Thread.Abort migration is needed here.**

Your code only uses `Thread.Start()`, `Thread.Join()`, and `Thread.Sleep()` — none of which are affected by the Thread.Abort removal in modern .NET. These APIs work identically on .NET 8. The code will compile and run correctly as-is on your target framework.

---

**Optional modernization (unrelated to Thread.Abort):** You could replace the manual thread management with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.Run` for cleaner code and better thread-pool utilization:

```csharp
public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    Parallel.ForEach(items, item => Process(item));
}
```

Or with cancellation support (useful if you later need to stop work on demand):

```csharp
public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items, CancellationToken token = default)
{
    Parallel.ForEach(items,
        new ParallelOptions { CancellationToken = token },
        item => Process(item));
}
```

But again — these are optional improvements, not required for the .NET 8 migration.
